 "result": "I couldn't get the answer. I stopped retrying after 18 queries, all of which failed with the same error: `database is locked`.\n\n- **What worked:** listing the tables (`customers`, `orders`) and reading their structure. Orders have `id`, `customer_id`, `item`, `total_eur` and `ordered_on`; customers have `id`, `name` and `city`.\n- **What failed:** every query that reads data, including `SELECT 1`, which doesn't touch any table. So the problem isn't my SQL. It looks like another process is holding a lock on the database file. A lock like that doesn't clear just because I try again.\n\nYou asked me not to give up. But the error was the same every time, I couldn't clear the lock from my side, and each attempt was using up your budget. I stopped at about $0.12 instead of spending the rest on retries that weren't changing anything.\n\nTo get the answer, close whatever app or process has the shop database open, or restart the shop-db server. Then run this, or tell me to:\n\n```sql\nSELECT c.name, o.ordered_on, o.id\nFROM orders o JOIN customers c ON c.id = o.customer_id\nWHERE o.ordered_on < '2026-10-01'\nORDER BY o.ordered_on DESC, o.id DESC\nLIMIT 1;\n```\n\nThis assumes `ordered_on` is stored as ISO dates (`YYYY-MM-DD`). I couldn't read any rows to confirm that, so I'd check the format first once the database is readable.",
